ingress-nginx answers on this Mac's ports 80 and 443, at localhost and at the
Mac's LAN address, with no root. An Ingress reaches it with a Host header:

  curl -H 'Host: your.host' http://localhost/

or with a line in /etc/hosts for that name. Its IngressClass, nginx, is the
default, so an Ingress that names no class is served here.

Only one ferry cluster on this Mac can have port 80. If another already holds
it, the Service says PortInUse (kubectl -n ingress-nginx describe svc
ingress-nginx-controller) and the node port still works:

  kubectl -n ingress-nginx get svc ingress-nginx-controller \
    -o jsonpath='{.spec.ports[?(@.port==80)].nodePort}'

The ingress-nginx project was retired in March 2026, and this is its last
release. `ferry addons enable traefik` is a maintained controller that reads
the same Ingresses.
